posts.body:
As always, our brave little dinosaur fixed RM's graphic shortcomings, this time for MZ! Thank you,
@Avery
! Now the forest tiles are usable.

@FirozKhan
These are MZ, so if you have already bought MZ you can use them in MV.
But if you don't have MZ you cannot use these

Good to see that
@Avery
is working on new stuff to improve upon the software. Keep up the good work, Avery!

Day 2: Pine Tree
There is only a snowy pine tree in the default RTP, and the snow covers so much, that unsnowing it meant drawing most of it from scratch... which on the other hand meant, now that I was on it anyways, I made a bigger one as well and the thinner one and added some trunk variation.
Now you can make pine forests, add some variation to your normal forest maps or add some random pines whereever they are needed :3
@WaywardMartian
And it continues ;3
@BrentBAM
Yeah, I felt like a door at the beginning was just fitting I'm glad you like it!
@Guardinthena
I had thought about wheather I should make an MZ calendar, but it just has the least resources yet and there are now also MZ users without MV x_x It was a tough decision, but at some point you maybe have MZ as well^^
@Lady_JJ
Awww, thank you! Yes, I felt like the door and the start of the calendar would like up perfectly!
@Monkeynugget
Psssst, don't let the Scarestaff organizers hear that ;D Even though it is a ton of work, this is something I enjoy a lot as well. Not sure about the blowing away, but we'll see
@Candacis
And I am still insecure when I look in the calendar folder xD True, a grey version might be very useful, maybe with a matching wall as well... I'll see what I can do^^ Door one is my favourite as well :3

I agree with
@Candacis
, the wolves would definitely look nice with your forest assets.  Also, I love dogs, and I can't help looking at these wolves and thinking 'aw, you poor thing!  Let me take you in, I will feed you, get you a good brush and bath and give you bone treats and name you Fluffy!'

I think there are some extremely useful icons there, especially the nail, matches, human figure, cheese, and pencil! My favorite in terms of the amount of detail is the paintbrush.
@M.I.A.
I do hope things get better!

What a beautiful dragon we have there!
@Avery
should be RM official artist....

Dear
@Avery
, what do yo usay about making a dinosaur charset? There is no even one dino in RPG Maker charsets, that would be super-awesome!

So many lovely gifts last year, but the dragon was my favorite. This is such a wonderful continuation,
@Avery
.

1str day and already such an AWESOME gift (I love that big dragon face and knight). Thank you
@Avery
, can't wait for other days.

2
Have you ever felt like the MZ organ was a bit underwhelming?
Well, time to bring your churches and temples to the next level with the instrument that matches the importance of the building!
And as Candacis suggested, I added some recolors for the dragons!
@Lady_JJ
Thanks! Yeah, it was one of my favs too, so that expansion was one of the first things I made for this year :3
@BeanCanDev
Nope, it is not, take a closer look and you'll find out who he actually is ;3
@Candacis
Thank you ♥ As you can see, I took that suggestion to heart :3
@GalacticGod
That is the whole purpose of thing thing, spreading some joy \o/ Thank you for the compliment :3
@Quexp
I am glad that you have a use for both of them :3 Feel free to share some screens when they found their spot!
@Lunesis
That would be cool! Make sure your heroes are not too underleveled when they meet him ;3
@fizzly
That is marketing, I needed to get you all hooked on the first day ;D I am glad you like them!
@slimmmeiske2
Thank you ♥ That is the whole plan, making everybody as happy as possible :3
@WanderingDudeBM
And now that you searched through it, here are new things!
@Aoi Ninami
That sounds really cool! I'd love to see some screens once that project takes shape!
@Sharm
~And here is more Dragons dragons dragons dragons!~ ♥
@M.I.A.
Yes, here we are again, glad to see you here as well :3 I hope this can make the holiday season somewhat more bearable ;3

3
When I had asked for suggestions for the calendar, someone mentioned vehicles and I thought MZ's RTP really lacked some hot air balloons and ship variations. So here are some brand new ways to explore maps or some model toys for your modern games!
My favourite is the tiny dragonboat with its little shields :3
Plus I made an edit to fit the knight from day 1, in case you want to face him in battle!
@jonthefox
Thank you :3
@tumsterfest
I am glad you like it, I think sometimes an impressive centerpiece can do a lot for a map!
@WaywardMartian
Don't forget, your opponents would have had it, too ;D
@fizzly
Thank you! The ice dragon is my favourite of these, too :3
@slimmmeiske2
True, though we now need some matching sprites for that scenario^^ Thank you!
@Candacis
You are welcome and I am looking forward to see the results!

Day
5
and we have the first advent sunday (actually the second, but the first within the calendar) and so I one of the larger things for you. As you can see, those are upscales and edits of those of the tiny MZ vehicles, and to be honest, a lot had to be drawn from scratch to make everything pretty and match the perspective. The bus is a fully new one that just matches the design of the tiny thing there.
So, those tiny toy cars are the defaults, the large ones are my work plus some neat recolors so you can quickly fill your parking lots!
@Aoi Ninami
I am sure you will come up with something cool to use it in :3 Thank you!
@jonthefox
Do you have an idea on where to use them already? :3
@Lunesis
That is difficult to explain in a few words, it is a mix of cloning and dodge and burn and copy and paste and using a solar curve to even everything out... acutally just how you would edit a photo, that is where I learned those tricks^^'
@Candacis
Thank you :3 I am glad you like the recolor you inspired ;D

@Avery
I feel like the last one (canyon landscape) would work so well for any kind of generic classic travel and save the world rpg
Speaking of title screens...A Christmas title screen would be awesome.

Today is St Nicholas Day and that means I have another special treat on day
6
!
A trea[n]t, if I may say so!
To be honest, most of the default big monsters don't really vibe with me, but that guy is super cool and what is more scary than being chased by a goddam tree? So instead of standing around, he can now walk in all directions.
Plus, I made transformation animation and even had the style change from pixealted charset to more painterly tileset with different light, so that you can have him blend in for your unsuspecting players... or just use him as tree, if you want, I mean, it is a perfectly fine tile on its own!
@Kentaro_
Thank you!
@jonthefox
That is true, especially since that is a really generic landscape ;3
@Candacis
Moving wheels for all of them?
I don't know, that would probably leand me down to the rabbit hole where I want to make the other angles as well and then we have january D;
@Lady_JJ
It would be nice if someone puts them to a good use :3 It is always difficult to decide what to make themewise, as while fantasy is the most popular, there are already a lot of resources... well, I hope I find some of these on some screens later :3

Oh my....I can't even tell how much I appreciate your AWESOME work,
@Avery
. Thank you so much ,as always.

Oh gosh, thank you so much
@Avery
! Beach thingies was my request, so happy that you've made them!! And the pot/pan/daikon icons, OMG OMG OMG. LOVE ALL.

Merry X-mas
@Avery
and everyone, I hope you had a great year and even if no, I hope the next one will be better or even better! Thank you for your work, everything is perfect.

Holy Crapolly!! What a wonderful BANG to end the Advent on!! Thank you so much for your contributions to this community
@Avery
! Merry Christmas to you.

Thank you for doing that
@Avery
. It is very much appreciated.

